📊 Outstanding Balance Dashboard

A Tableau dashboard analyzing client outstanding balances against interest rates and reporting dates, developed as part of an Internshala Trainings data visualization assignment.

Overview

This project explores a client balance dataset to uncover patterns between interest rates and outstanding balances, and to surface the highest-exposure clients over time. The dashboard was built in Tableau Public and is designed to be interactive, allowing viewers to filter results by reporting date.

Objectives

The dashboard was built to answer three core analytical questions:

#	Question
1	What is the distribution of outstanding balances across different interest rates?
2	Is there a correlation between interest rates and outstanding balances?
3	Who are the top 5 clients by outstanding balance, and how does this ranking shift when filtered by reporting date?
Dataset

File: Tableau_Dataset.xlsx

Field	Description
Product Description	Name/type of the financial product
Client Name	Client identifier
Balance Outstanding	Outstanding balance amount
Interest Rate	Applicable interest rate
Reporting Date	Date of the balance record
Client Code	Unique client code
Dashboard Components
Sheet	Chart Type	Purpose
Balance Distribution	Bar chart	Shows how outstanding balances are distributed across interest rate bands
Rate vs Balance	Scatter plot + trend line	Visualizes the relationship and correlation strength between interest rate and balance outstanding
Top 5 Clients	Ranked bar chart	Highlights the top 5 clients by outstanding balance, filterable by reporting date
Key Insights

To be completed after reviewing the dashboard output — summarize the shape of the distribution, the direction and strength of the correlation, and which clients consistently rank in the top 5.

Tech Stack
Tableau Public — dashboard design and visualization
Microsoft Excel — data source and preprocessing
